# UI test: a shared borrow and an exclusive access that overlap (SC0330).
#
# Rule 4, reported against an *access* rather than against a second borrow:
# writing a place something else holds shared is the violation, and
# `region-inference.md` §3 step 4 as written quantifies over borrows only.
# `science-regions`'s `access` §1 is the amendment, and this is its shape.
#
# The borrow ends at its last use, so the same program with the two last lines
# swapped compiles. That is Decision 1's whole point and it is why the third
# span — *"the first borrow is still needed here"* — is the load-bearing one.

type Doc:
    title: Int

def main():
    let mutable doc be Doc(title: 0)
    let shared be borrowed doc
    doc.title be 1
    print(shared.title)
